{"raw": {"https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=62108": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Accounting", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Accounting Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Accounting Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Accounting Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Jul 30, 2015 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position\u00a0ID: 62108 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Business Programs of the School of Business and Leadership at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks part-time Adjunct Accounting Instructors beginning Fall 2015 term (August 30, 2015). The course(s) to be taught: Financial Accounting (Principles of Accounting and Intermediate Accounting) Taxation Auditing Cost Accounting or Managerial Accounting Prepare syllabi, lectures, assignments, and assessments, as appropriate to the course under the supervision of a lead professor who will provide a sample syllabus and select the textbook(s) for the course.\u00a0Be available for individual student assistance (outside class time) at least one hour per week per section, and/or respond to telephone or electronic communication from students within 24-48 hours. Requirements: Ph. D in Accounting preferred \u00a0OR Master's degree in Accounting or related business field from an accredited institution of higher learning and be currently licensed as a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) within the State of Texas or be able to obtain reciprocity licensure before the start of the academic term Professional experience in the Accounting field (significant industry experience or professional accounting firms) Available to teach in a variety of modalities:\u00a0 face to face classes or online classes Available to teach Face to Face classes in the following formats: traditional day classes, evening classes, or weekend classes Prior experience working or teaching in one or more of the topic areas and course formats described. Commitment to excellence in teaching, student centeredness, and (where applicable) classroom use of technology.\u00a0Teaching accounting classes at the university level is strongly preferred Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Professor Michelle I. Avila, Associate Professor of Accounting\u00a0and Accounting Program Head (210) 528-7188 or\u00a0miavila@ollusa.edu Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae, Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=81252": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Applied Social and Cultural Sciences", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Applied Social and Cultural Sciences Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Applied Social and Cultural Sciences Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Applied Social and Cultural Sciences Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Feb 7, 2017 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 81252 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The School of Professional Studies invites applications from qualified individuals to teach in the undergraduate Sociology program at the San Antonio Campus.\u00a0 Mapping the Social World course is scheduled to be taught on Mondays and Wednesdays, 11:00 a.m. - 12:15 p.m. in a traditional format. Responsibilities: Prepare syllabi, lectures, assignments, and assessments, as appropriate to the course under the supervision of the department chair or program head director who will provide a sample syllabus and select the textbook(s) for the course.\u00a0 Must be available for individual student assistance (outside class time) at least one hour per week per section, and/or respond to telephone or electronic communication from students within 24-48 hours. Requirements: Minimum - Master's Degree in the specific field of Sociology or an approved equivalent degree in the social sciences. Applicants with a Master's degree in Geography will be considered. Preferred - Doctoral degree in Sociology or related field.\u00a0 Knowledge and Experience in Geographic Information Systems are required. Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Renelinda A. Bressler, PhD - Applied Social and Cultural Science Department rabressler@ollusa.edu Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae, Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=47360": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Art (multiple positions)", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Art (multiple positions) Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Art (multiple positions) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Art (multiple positions) Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Humanities and Social Sciences Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Mar 11, 2014 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 47360 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Salazar-Escobedo School at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks Adjunct Instructors of Art to be included in the general pool of candidates from which qualified part-time faculty will be selected for the upcoming academic term.\u00a0 The deadline for application is November 20 for consideration for the Spring semester and June 20 for the Fall semester. The courses to be taught (contingent upon enrollment): Art Appreciation Design I-\u00a0Two Dimensional Design II- Color Theory Design III-Three Dimensional Design Design IV - Four-Dimensional Design Drawing I & II Painting I & II Watercolor Ceramics I & II Digital Imaging I & II Digital Photography I & II Printmaking I & II Sculpture I & II Graphics Narrative and Sequential Art Teaching Art Self-Portrait 21st Century Global Perspectives Art History Mexican American Visual Arts Barrio Art & Popular Culture History of Modern Art Contemporary Art History Afrika: The 3rd Root of Mexico \u00b7 Art of Ancient Americas \u00b7 Womxn, Gender, Social Change in Art \u00b7 Art of Chicanx Civil Rights Movement \u00b7 Senior Exhibition Seminar Requirements: Master's Degree in Art (from a regionally accredited college or university) or in a related sub-field. The preferred candidates will have an MFA in Studio Art or an MA in Art Education. Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Suzy Gonzalez, Program Head, Visual Arts, sbgonzalez@ollusa.edu Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae , Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=46957": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Biology Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Biology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Biology Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Mathematics and Sciences Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Mar 3, 2014 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 46957 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Mathematics and Sciences Department at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks a part-time Biology Instructors beginning Fall 2016. Duties and Responsibilities include: Preparing and presenting lectures and labs under the direction of the course and laboratory coordinators; maintaining availability to students during the week (at least one hour per week). The course(s) to be taught: Introduction to Evolution. This is an online course for non-majors. Introduction to Life Sciences lecture and lab. This is our freshman level introductory course for non-majors. It is part of the university's General Education curriculum. General Biology I and II lecture and lab. This is our freshman sequence for biology majors. Human Anatomy and Physiology I and II lecture and lab. Molecular/Cell Biology Requirements: The candidates should have at least a MS in Biology or a related field. A PhD in Biology or related field is preferred. Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Dr. Alfredo Vaquiax, Mathematics & Sciences Chair, advaquiax-alvarado@ollusa.edu. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae , Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=58097": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Chemistry (Faculty Pool)", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Chemistry (Faculty Pool) Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Chemistry (Faculty Pool) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Chemistry (Faculty Pool) Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Mar 24, 2015 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 58097 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Mathematics and Sciences Department at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks part-time (Adjunct) Chemistry Instructors. Duties and Responsibilities include: Preparing and presenting lectures and labs under the direction of the course and laboratory coordinators; maintaining availability to students during the week (at least one hour per week). The course(s) to be taught: Lectures and labs in General Chemistry and Organic Chemistry Requirements: The candidate must have a Ph.D. in Chemistry; however a Master's degree in Chemistry or at least 18 graduate hours in chemistry will be considered. Experience teaching Organic Chemistry is preferred. Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Dr. Alfredo Vaquiax, Mathematics & Sciences Chair, advaquiax-alvarado@ollusa.edu. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae, Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205965": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of CISS - Online", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of CISS - Online Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of CISS - Online Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of CISS - Online Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CISS Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Oct 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 205965 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The CISS department invites applications from qualified individuals to teach one or two sections of undergraduate computer information systems courses.\u00a0 The CISS department invites applications from qualified individuals to teach one or two sections of undergraduate Computer Information Systems courses. Class schedules may vary, and sections available for adjunct faculty to teach will be offered online. Courses in several topic areas may be available, including Database Analysis and Design, Management of Information Systems, and Information Systems Security. Online courses are asynchronous. Requirements: Minimum - Master's degree in information systems, Computer Science, Cybersecurity or related discipline; experience working and/or teaching in one or more of the topic areas and course formats described above; commitment to excellence in teaching, student-centeredness, and (where applicable) classroom use of technology, certification in related area(s). Preferred - Doctoral degree in one of the fields listed above, Information Systems, Computer Science, Cybersecurity or closely related discipline Review of applications is ongoing while position(s) remain unfilled. Additional Information: For questions about the application process, contact: Human Resources Office at 210-431-3970 or email: hrteam@ollusa.edu. For questions about the position description, responsibilities, or qualifications, contact Professor Kelly Roberts-Cooper, program coordinator of the CISS department at klroberts-copper@ollusa.edu. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Our Lady of the Lake University is an Affirmative Action, Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to diversity within its community. In pursuit of that, we actively encourage diversity among applicants for this position. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: cover letter, curriculum vitae, copies of official transcripts, reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=105609": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Communication Sciences and Disorders", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Communication Sciences and Disorders Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Communication Sciences and Disorders Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Communication Sciences and Disorders Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Communication Disorders Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Dec 10, 2018 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position\u00a0ID: 105609 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Woolfolk School of Communication Sciences and Disorders at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks Adjunct Lecturer in Communication Disorders.\u00a0For Fall, Spring, and Summer terms, the requirement is to teach one undergraduate or graduate course in the areas of speech-language pathology or audiology. Requirements: Minimum requirements: Masters or PhD in communication sciences/disorders or a related field. Preferred requirements: Experience teaching communication sciences in a regionally accredited institution of higher education; two years post Master's degree practice in speech language pathology or audiology and ASHA certification of clinical competence (CCC). Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Dr. Christine Carmichael, Director,\u00a0ccarmichael@ollusa.edu Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: letter of Interest denoting position for which applying Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=80597": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Counseling", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Counseling Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Counseling Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Counseling Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Education Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Jan 18, 2017 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 80597 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. The Master of Arts in Counseling (MAC) program at Our Lady of the Lake University is accredited by the Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs (CACREP). Job Description: The Department of Counseling in the College of Professional Studies at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio, TX invites applications from qualified individuals to teach online synchronous/asynchronous graduate counseling courses. Preference for clinical training coursework (add to qualifications/preferred qualifications): Preference will be given to applicants with demonstrated strength and teaching experience in clinical training coursework (e.g., practicum, internship, counseling techniques, or clinical supervision). Other courses in several topic areas may be available, including the following: School Counseling Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling Mental Health Counseling Addictions Counseling Research Couples & Family Therapy Assessment Requirements: Applicants must hold an earned Doctorate degree in Counselor Education (CACREP accredited program graduates are desired) or a related field; must have a thorough knowledge and understanding of current best practices in the specific fields of: Clinical Mental Health Counseling School Counseling Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling Qualifications: Background in counseling or previous teaching at the university level preferred. Willingness to teach courses in a variety of formats including traditional, weekend and online. Must be student centered. Must demonstrate outstanding presentation/teaching skills. Must incorporate technology and model best teaching practices. Applicants for School Counseling must have at least one the following: Texas School Counseling Certification, LPC, NCC Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Dr.\u00a0Melissa Shiplett-Jupe, Chair, Department of Counseling Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment ( must indicate topic area applying for on the\u00a0application section\u00a0\"position applying for\"; e.g. if applying to teach Special Education courses, indicate Special Education on academic application) and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae, Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=153283": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Economics (San Antonio)", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Economics (San Antonio) Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Economics (San Antonio) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Economics (San Antonio) Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: Sep 15, 2022 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 153283 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Business Programs department at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks a part-time Adjunct Economics Instructor beginning Fall 2022 term (August 2022). The course(s) to be taught: Undergraduate and/or Graduate courses in Economics, Econometrics, and Health Economics. Ability to teach a course in Data Analytics is preferred. Prepare syllabi, lectures, assignments, and assessments as appropriate to the course under the supervision of a lead professor who will provide a sample syllabus and select the textbook(s) for the course. Be available for individual student assistance (outside class time) at least one hour per week per section, and/or respond to telephone or electronic communication from students within 24-48 hours. Requirements: Master's degree in Economics or 18 semester graduate hours in Economics at a minimum. Preferred - Ph.D. in Economics Experience teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Economics Professional experience and/or credentials related to Economics are a plus. Significant industry experience is preferred Available to teach in a variety of modalities:\u00a0 face to face classes or online classes Available to teach Face to Face classes in the following formats: traditional day classes, evening classes, or weekend classes Prior experience working or teaching in one or more of the topic areas and course formats described. Commitment to excellence in teaching, student-centeredness, and (where applicable) classroom use of technology. Additional Information: For questions about the application process, contact: Human Resources Office at 210-431-3970 or email: hrteam@ollusa.edu. For questions about the position, contact: Professor Michelle Avila, Chair, Department of Business, miavila@ollusa.edu OLLU seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff, and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: Letter of Interest denoting position for which applying. Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae. Copies of official transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying. Listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=79229": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Education", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Education Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Education Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Education Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Nov 30, 2016 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 79229 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The School of Professional Studies Education Department at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio invites applications from qualified individuals to teach undergraduate and graduate education courses. Courses in several topic areas may be available, including the following: Bilingual Education Curriculum and Instruction Special Education Literacy and Reading ESL Requirements: Applicants must hold an earned Master's or Doctorate degree in Education or a related field; must have a thorough knowledge and understanding of current best practices in the specific fields of: Bilingual ESL Reading Literacy Curriculum and Instruction ( including teacher education and pedagogy) Special Education Qualifications: Background in education or previous teaching at the university level preferred. Texas Teacher Certification preferred. PK-12 classroom teaching experience preferred. Willingness to teach courses in a variety of formats including traditional, weekend and online. Must be student centered. Must demonstrate outstanding presentation/teaching skills. Must incorporate technology and model best teaching practices. Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Dr. Alycia D. Maurer, Chair, Department of Education. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment (must indicate topic area applying for on the\u00a0application section\u00a0\"position applying for\"; e.g. if applying to teach Special Education courses, indicate Special Education on academic application) and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae, Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=46962": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of English", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of English Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of English Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of English Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Mar 3, 2014 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 46962 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Salazar-Escobedo School at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks Adjunct Instructors of English to be included in the general pool of candidates from which qualified part-time faculty will be selected for the upcoming academic term. The deadline for application is November 20 for consideration for the Spring semester and June 20 for the Fall semester. Responsibilities include : preparing and presenting lectures and writing activities under the direction of the Composition Coordinator; maintaining availability to students during the week (at least one hour per week); a willingness to participate in ongoing faculty development; and attending a mandatory Summer Faculty Workshop. The courses to be taught may include: ENGL 1313- Composition I: An introduction to academic writing, depending on enrollment and needed sections. ENGL 1314 - Composition II, depending on enrollment and needed sections. Traditional Humanities sections and/or Writing in the Discipline (WID) Courses specializing in STEM, Business, Psychology, and Social Work. General Education Literature Courses (majors and non-majors, freshman and sophomore level), depending on enrollment and needed sections. Sophomore level literature, depending on enrollment and needed sections. Requirements: Requirements: MA in English, terminal degree preferred Specialization in Composition and Rhetoric preferred Experience teaching first-year, first-generation college students Additional desirable qualifications include: Effective integration of technology to facilitate student learning Skills in assessing students learning Willingness to work with the Composition Curriculum Team Ability to communicate effectively with a culturally diverse community Ability to teach face-to-face, asynchronous online, or hybrid Additional Information: Contract renewal is contingent upon evidence of teaching effectiveness. For questions about the position contact: Prof. Laura Petersen, Assistant Professor of Professional Writing and Communication English Composition Coordinator, lapetersen@ollusa.edu, 210-431-6587. Employent with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following : letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae , Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=75026": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Graduate Psychology", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Graduate Psychology Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Graduate Psychology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Graduate Psychology Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Aug 5, 2016 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 75026 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Psychology Department at Our Lady of the Lake University is currently seeking applicants for an Adjunct (Part-Time) Instructor for the graduate programs in psychology (PsyD in Counseling Psychology and MS in Psychology with concentrations in School Psychology, and Family Therapy). Preferred areas of expertise include theory and practice of psychotherapy (individual, couple, family, and group), supervision of practicum students, consultation, psychological assessment and diagnosis, lifespan development, ethics, cognition, behavioral neuroscience, and research methods. Requirements: A minimum of a doctoral degree in psychology, school psychology, Marriage and Family Therapy or a related area along with clinical and/or applied experience and demonstrated effectiveness in teaching required. Licensure as a Marriage and Family Therapist and AAMFT Approved Supervisor status is preferred for teaching courses in the Family Therapy concentration of the MS program.\u00a0 Licensure as a psychologist is preferred for teaching in the PsyD program. Additional Information: For questions about the application process, contact: Human Resources at 210-431-3970 or email: dahealy@ollusa.edu. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: Letter of Interest denoting position for which applying. Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae. Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying. Listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=175291": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of History", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of History Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of History Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of History Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: College of Arts & Sciences Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: May 1, 2024 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Position\u00a0ID: 175291 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Department of Humanities and Social Sciences at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks Adjunct History Instructors to be included in the general pool of candidates from which qualified part-time faculty will be selected for the upcoming academic term. The deadline for application is December 1 for consideration for the Spring semester and July 1 for the Fall semester. Primary responsibility will be to teach freshman-level survey classes that fulfil the University's general education requirement in history. Other duties may include teaching course for history majors and minors (contingent upon enrollment) Preference for teaching online or in person on the San Antonio campus may be specified in the cover letter. Enrollment in face-to-face classes is usually capped at thirty students and in on-line classes (both synchronous and asynchronous) at thirty-five. The course(s) to be taught may include: World History 1355 and 1356 (to 1500/from 1450) US History 1301 and 1302 (to/from 1865) Requirements: Minimum: Master's degree (MA) in History Additional desirable qualifications include: Previous teaching experience at the post-secondary level, particularly survey courses similar to those stated above; The ability to communicate effectively with a culturally diverse community; Creativity and innovation in classroom instruction; Effective integration of technology to facilitate student learning. Additional Information: Contract renewal is contingent upon evidence of teaching effectiveness. For questions about the position, please contact:\u00a0Dr. Jessica Hajek, Chair Department of Humanities and Social Sciences, jchajek@ollusa.edu, or Dr. Christopher Rose, History Program Head, csrose@ollusa.edu. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online\u00a0Application for Academic Employment\u00a0and\u00a0attach the following: A letter of Interest\u00a0(cover letter) clearly stating which course(s) you are interested/able to teach and in which format(s) (in person/online); Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae; Copies of all transcripts\u00a0reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying (unofficial transcripts may submitted with the application; official transcripts will be required before a contract can be issued); A list of three professional references (letters not required at the time of application). For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time.\u00a0Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=75858": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Kinesiology", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Kinesiology Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Kinesiology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next 