., Department Chair, jchajek@ollusa.edu OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: Letter of Interest denoting position for which applying. Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae. Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying. Listing of three professional references. Two current letters of recommendation emailed to jchajek@ollusa.edu For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=140051": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Theology", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Theology Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Theology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Theology Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: College of Arts & Sciences Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: Dec 1, 2021 Closes: Dec 31, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Contract Position\u00a0ID: 140051 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Department of Humanities and Social Sciences at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks Adjunct Theology Instructors to be included in the general pool of candidates from which qualified part-time faculty will be selected for the upcoming academic term. The deadline for application is November 20 for consideration for the Spring semester and June 20 for the Fall semester. Primary responsibility will be to teach general education courses in the Theology & Spiritual Action program. The course(s) to be taught may include: \u00b7 THSA 1300 The Catholic Imagination \u00b7 THSA 1310 Introduction to Spirituality and Providence \u00b7 THSA 1320 Reading the Bible Requirements: Minimum: master's degree (MA, MDiv, etc.) in Theology, Divinity, Ministry, or Religious Studies or Doctorate degree in closely related field (e.g., Philosophy, History, Sociology, Anthropology, etc.) with at least 18 hours in theology or religious studies. Generalist background and ability to teach a variety of subfields. Enthusiasm for connecting music to first-generation college students, both majors and non-majors, and deep commitment to the mission and identity of the University. Willingness and ability to teach either in person or online and employing service-learning pedagogies. Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Jacob Friesenhahn, Ph.D., Program Head for Theology and Spiritual Action, jhfriesenhahn@ollusa.edu . OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: Letter of Interest denoting position for which applying. Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae. Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying. Listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=148463": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Finance Instructor", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Adjunct Finance Instructor Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Adjunct Finance Instructor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Adjunct Finance Instructor Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Jun 2, 2022 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 148463 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Business Programs department at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio seeks a part-time Adjunct Finance Instructor beginning Fall 2022 term (August 2022). The course(s) to be taught: Undergraduate and/or Graduate courses in Finance Prepare syllabi, lectures, assignments, and assessments as appropriate to the course under the supervision of a lead professor who will provide a sample syllabus and select the textbook(s) for the course. Be available for individual student assistance (outside class time) at least one hour per week per section, and/or respond to telephone or electronic communication from students within 24-48 hours. Requirements: Ph. D in Finance preferred OR Master's degree in Finance. 18 semester graduate hours in Finance at a minimum. Experience teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Finance. Professional experience and/or certification (CFA, CFP, FRM) in the Finance field (significant industry experience). Available to teach in a variety of modalities:\u00a0 face to face classes or online classes. Available to teach Face to Face classes in the following formats: traditional day classes, evening classes, or weekend classes. Prior experience working or teaching in one or more of the topic areas and course formats described. Commitment to excellence in teaching, student-centeredness, and (where applicable) classroom use of technology. Additional Information: For questions about the position, contact: Professor Michelle Avila, Chair, Department of Business, miavila@ollusa.edu OLLU seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff, and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: Letter of Interest denoting position for which applying. Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae. Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying. Listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time via online application. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=145579": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Business Analytics (Online)", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Business Analytics (Online) Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Instructor of Business Analytics (Online) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Instructor of Business Analytics (Online) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Business Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Apr 20, 2022 Closes: May 31, 2034 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 145579 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Department of Business invites applications from qualified individuals to teach courses in the Master of Science in Business Analytics program.\u00a0 All classes available are offered online.\u00a0 Courses in several topic areas may be available, including Data Analytics with Python, Data Science and Machine Learning, Dashboard, Scorecard and Visualization, and a Capstone Project in Business Analytics. Responsibilities: Prepare lectures, computer lab activities, assignments, and assessments, as appropriate to the course under the supervision of a lead professor who will provide a sample syllabus and select the textbook(s) for the course. Be available for individual student assistance (outside class time) at least one hour per week per section, and/or respond to telephone or electronic communication from students within 24-48 hours. Requirements: Minimum - Master's degree in Data Science, Business Administration, Computer Science, or related discipline; experience working and/or teaching in one or more of the topic areas and course formats described above; commitment to excellence in teaching, student-centeredness, and (where applicable) classroom use of technology. Preferred - Doctoral degree in one of the fields listed above; certification in related area(s), particularly Data Analytics or related field. Review of applications is ongoing while position(s) remain unfilled. Additional Information: For questions about the application process, contact: Human Resources Office at 210-431-3970 or email: hrteam@ollusa.edu. For questions about the position description, responsibilities, or qualifications, contact Professor Michelle I. Avila, Chair, School of Business and Technology, at miavila@ollusa.edu. Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Our Lady of the Lake University is an Affirmative Action, Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to diversity within its community. In pursuit of that, we actively encourage diversity among applicants for this position. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: cover letter, curriculum vitae, copies of official transcripts, reflecting receipt of Master's or PhD degree in discipline for which applying, and listing of three professional references. For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=199257": {"title": "Assistant / Associate Professor of Psychology", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Assistant / Associate Professor of Psychology Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant / Associate Professor of Psychology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant / Associate Professor of Psychology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: Apr 8, 2026 Closes: Nov 30, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 199257 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: The Psychology Department at Our Lady of the Lake University in San Antonio invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant / Associate Professor rank to primarily serve the APA-accredited Counseling Psychology PsyD program beginning August 2027. The OLLU Psychology Department offers the following degrees: PsyD in Counseling Psychology and MS in Psychology, with concentrations in Marriage and Family Therapy and School Psychology. The mission of the psychology graduate programs is to prepare culturally competent professionals who are skilled in providing strengths-based psychotherapy to individuals, couples and families from diverse backgrounds. Graduate students may complete a certificate in providing psychological services in Spanish. The Psychology Department operates a community-based clinic that serves a low-income, multi-ethnic, population presenting with wide-ranging concerns. The clinic offers opportunities for innovative practice, training, and research Position duties include, but are not limited to: Teaching masters and doctoral students from Strength-Based, Solution-Focused, Narrative and/or Collaborative Theories with an emphasis on multiculturalism and social justice. Providing \"live\" supervision (from a Systemic theory-base) to a weekly therapy team at the university-sponsored clinic. Chairing and serving on dissertation committees. Academic advising and mentoring of students. Evaluating student comprehensive and clinical qualifying exams. Engaging in program activities such as student recruitment, interviews, program evaluation. Conducting and engaging students in research and scholarly activities. Serving on university committees. Possible courses to be taught may include: (courses may be negotiated) Assessment Courses Life Planning and Career Development Human Development Across the Lifespan Research Methods Cognition & Emotion Behavioral Neuroscience Requirements: Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Counseling Psychology from an APA accredited program; Licensed or License-Eligible as a Psychologist in Texas Expertise in teaching graduate & doctoral students & Expertise in supervision Expertise in qualitative research methods Expertise in brief, systemic, strengths-based approaches to psychotherapy - Solution-Focused Brief Therapy, Narrative Therapy Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching and supervising graduate and doctoral students AAMFT approved supervisor or eligible to become a supervisor in training Proficient in Spanish Licensed as a psychologist in Texas within one year or hire (if not licensed) Additional Information: For questions about the position contact: Dr Deborah Hendren at DkHendren@ollusa.edu Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Academic Employment and attach the following: letter of Interest denoting position for which applying, Resume and/or Curriculum Vitae , Copies of all transcripts reflecting receipt of terminal degree in discipline for which applying, two letters of recommendation , and a listing of three professional references . For consideration for Academic Employment, all materials above must be submitted together and at one time. Incomplete packets for academic employment will not be considered. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200095": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Communication Sciences and Disorders Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: May 1, 2026 Closes: Dec 31, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Position\u00a0ID: 200095 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: About the Woolfolk School Our Lady of the Lake University's communication disorders program was founded in 1955 and is proud of a long history providing the highest quality training of speech-language pathologists throughout San Antonio, Texas and the United States. We are particularly proud of our pioneering training in bilingual and multi-cultural services, and our curriculum pays special attention to cultural competence and cultural humility. The Woolfolk School of Communication Sciences and Disorders was named in 2017 after its founder, Dr. Elizabeth Carrow Woolfolk, OLLU alumna and internationally recognized scholar in the field of communication sciences, and her husband, Robert M. Woolfolk. OLLU is a leader in the field of communication disorders and established its first program more than 70 years ago, combining professional training with clinical service in the Harry Jersig Speech-Language-Hearing Center. The Woolfolk School offers bachelor's, master's, and doctorate degrees in Communication Sciences and Disorders/Speech-Language Pathology as well as a post-baccalaureate leveling program. OLLU's graduate training program has been accredited in speech-language pathology since 1969 by the Council on Academic Accreditation of the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA). Job Summary The Woolfolk School of Communication Sciences and Disorders seeks a full-time, tenure track faculty member in speech-language pathology beginning in fall 2026. Responsibilities include teaching graduate courses in communication sciences and disorders, as well as opportunities to supervise theses at the master's level and capstone projects in the clinical doctorate program. The faculty member will be expected to teach in respective area(s) of specialty within the field. Additional responsibilities include student advisement, involvement in school and university committees, research in the faculty's area(s) of interest, and clinical supervision of graduate students evaluating and treating client disorders that align with faculty area(s) of expertise. The Woolfolk School of Communication Sciences and Disorders is housed within the College of Professional Studies and includes the Harry Jersig Speech-Language-Hearing Center. The Center offers diagnostic and treatment services to children and adults for a variety of communication and swallowing disorders, and includes labs in child language, multicultural diversity, and voice & swallowing. The school consists of a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) in Communication Sciences and Disorders Program, a Communication Sciences and Disorders Post-Baccalaureate Leveling Program, a Master of Arts (M.A.) in Communication Sciences and Disorders Program, and a Clinical Doctorate in Speech-Language Pathology Doctorate (SLPD) program. Requirements: Qualified candidates will have obtained a Ph.D./Ed.D. degree in communication sciences and disorders or a related field. ABD candidates for Ph.D./Ed.D. will be considered. The selected candidate must be able to obtain a TX licensure for speech-language pathology and hold ASHA certification in speech-language pathology. The position will begin fall 2026. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. OLLU is a Catholic university that seeks to attract, develop, and retain the highest quality faculty, staff, and administrators.\u00a0 OLLU is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Application Instructions: Questions about this position should be addressed to: Faculty Search Committee Chair: Christine Carmichael, Ph.D., CCC-SLP Email: ccarmichael@ollusa.edu Application Deadline: Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205961": {"title": "Assistant Director for Residence Life", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director for Residence Life Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director for Residence Life Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director for Residence Life Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residence Life Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Oct 20, 2026 Closes: Dec 8, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 205961 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: The Assistant Director of Residence Life (ADRL) supports the Director of Residence Life (DRL) in the administration, assessment, and daily operation of the University's housing and residence life program. The position provides leadership for residential operations, student development, staff supervision, conduct and crisis response, occupancy and housing processes, facilities coordination, assessment, and departmental initiatives. The Assistant Director serves as a key operational leader within Residence Life and assumes the Director's delegated responsibilities when appropriate. The position assists with supervising live-in Residence Life Coordinators (RLC), Graduate Assistant (GA), and Resident Assistants (RA's). \u00a0The Assistant Director lives on campus and receives a salary, furnished on-campus apartment, and meal plan as part of their compensation package. Performance Metrics: Residential Student Retention and Satisfaction - Monitor residential retention, early move-outs, housing cancellations, resident feedback, and satisfaction data; identify trends and recommend improvements. Residence Hall Operations - Monitor occupancy, room assignments, openings/closings, work orders, health and safety processes, key accountability, and unresolved facility concerns. Staff Performance and Development - Evaluate RLC/GA/RA job performance, training completion, staff communication, programming effectiveness, and response to student needs. Student Conduct and Risk Management - Monitor timeliness, accuracy, documentation, and resolution of conduct, crisis, and safety matters. Essential Functions: The role assists the Director in the leadership and administration of a comprehensive residential experience to promote student success, engagement, and retention. This includes direct supervision, coaching, training, and development of RLCs, GAs, and RAs within their respective areas. Additionally, the role oversees several internal or operational processes and programs that shape the residential experience. Student Resident Support Serves in the regular \"on-call\" supervisory rotation and responds to emergencies, crises, safety concerns, and incidents affecting residential students and facilities, while observing safety and risk management measures. Ensure the safety of the students by reporting issues, tracking key inventory, working with the University Police Department (UPD), and enforcing the rules outlined in the resident handbook and student handbook. Work cooperatively with other campus units such as UPD, Counseling Services, Student Involvement, and Student Affairs to ensure the delivery of essential services to students. Mediate roommate conflicts that escalate beyond the Resident Assistant's intervention efforts. Resident Assistant Staff Coordinate the recruiting, interviewing, selecting, training, supervising, and evaluating of RA staff. Oversee the development and implementation of residential education programming model. Supervise and support assigned RAs by reviewing, evaluating, and approving program plans and bulletin board submissions; providing constructive guidance on programming initiatives and content; monitoring compliance with established deadlines and expectations; and assessing program effectiveness. Conduct group weekly meetings and bi-weekly one-on-one meetings with RA staff. Coordinate the on-duty SOC and RA on-duty schedule (for their area). Oversee the completion of student employee onboarding paperwork and submission to the Student Employment Office; file internal employee compliance training records. Administrative Functions Assume delegated departmental responsibilities and provide leadership for Residence Life operations when the DRL is unavailable. Serve as the operational liaison between the DRL and assigned Residence Life staff. Create and maintain Residence Life forms for internal operational documents. Assist with resident check-in/check-out in StarRez and ID activation in Velocity. Assist with planning for semester openings, closings, holiday periods, emergency situations, and other high-impact housing operations. Ensure accurate key inventory, that is completed by the GA. Coordinate residence hall access procedures, emergency preparedness, health and safety check processes, and security practices; serve as a member of the University Emergency Response Team. Develop and maintain departmental procedures, calendars, tracking systems, reports, and documentation for assigned areas. Track Residence Life programs (including RA and Department programs), health and safety checks, and other required data for reports on their assigned area. Collect and analyze operational data, including occupancy, retention, conduct, resident satisfaction, facilities, and staff performance, and provide reports and recommendations to the DRL; review operational data and resident feedback to identify trends, risks, service gaps, and opportunities for improvement. Serve as a Student Conduct Officer for Student Affairs and the Office of Residence Life. Investigate and manage student conduct matters, roommate conflicts, policy violations, and student concerns; ensures appropriate and timely documentation, communication, follow-up, and referral; report Title IX and student conduct issues through the OLLU webpage or Maxient. Determine Residence Life violation sanctions (e.g., pet, health and safety issues). Assist the DRL and/or Office Manager the comprehensive administration of all summer camps, conferences, and groups visiting the university and utilizing the residence halls. Review and approve social media content before posting. Assist with monitoring departmental expenditures and ensuring assigned activities remain within established fiscal parameters. Utilize StarRez to assist with room and board assignment, cancellation, and waitlist processes, and work with Financial Aid, Student Business Office, and other offices to resolve housing and meal plan issues affecting students when the office manager or DRL is not present. Manage the department email when the office manager is not present. Attend all division meetings and seminars as scheduled and attend weekly and impromptu meetings with the Residence Life pro staff. Facilities Management Oversee daily hall operations within the assigned residential area, including conducting routine facility walkthroughs, coordinating and monitoring work orders through completion, facilitating timely communication with residents, and maintaining a consistent and visible staff presence. Coordinates with Facilities, housekeeping, vendors, and other campus partners regarding maintenance, work orders, repairs, and residence hall conditions; follows up on unresolved issues. Assists with residence hall openings and closings, room changes, occupancy management, room inventories, floor charts, key inventories, and other housing operations. Complete furniture inventory and damage reports for Residence Life areas at the end of the school year or as needed. Assist with replacing furniture at the end of the school year. Additional Responsibilities Serves as a liaison from Residence Life to assigned campus departments and external partners. Provides Residence Life information during student orientation, recruitment events, tours, and special programs. Supports departmental marketing, communication, and student engagement initiatives. Assists with the development and evaluation of Residence Life policies, procedures, programs, and services. Provides support for Lake Day Orientation, Blue Nation Welcome, and other Student Affairs events. Participates in other university activities and programs as requested and assigned. Performs other related duties as assigned by the DRL, Assistant Vice President for Student Affairs, or Vice President for Student Affairs. Requirements: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to live on-campus and encompass a rotational, evening/weekend \"on call\" supervisory responsibility. Ability to work flexible hours, with busier periods at certain times of the semester, including evenings, weekends, holidays, and on-call responsibilities as needed. Strong knowledge of residence life, housing operations, student development, and residential education. Knowledge of student conduct processes, crisis response, safety, risk management, and student support practices. Demonstrated supervisory, coaching, conflict-resolution, and staff-development skills. Strong organizational, analytical, project-management, and problem-solving skills. Ability to analyze operational data and translate findings into recommendations and process improvements. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, public relations, and networking skills. Ability to exercise independent and sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and respond effectively under pressure. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office and ability to learn and effectively use StarRez and other University systems. Ability to meet the OLLU and Residence Life staff standards for on-campus and workplace environment safety for self and any family or guests on property. Ability to lift at least 20 pounds and be able to quickly move between housing buildings during emergencies. Must be able to perform essential job duties across multiple campus facilities and building floors, including older buildings that may have limited accessibility and no elevator service. Education and Experience Master's degree in education, psychology, social work, student affairs, higher education, or a related field required; a bachelor's degree plus four years of related full-time experience may substitute for the master's degree. Minimum of three years of progressively responsible post-bachelor's experience in residence life, housing, student affairs, or a related higher education environment required. One year of supervisory experience required. Experience with student conduct/judicial processes required. Experience planning, implementing, and evaluating student development or residential programs required. Experience with housing management software, preferably StarRez. Experience using operational data, assessment results, or student feedback to improve services is strongly preferred. Must live on-campus in the furnished apartment. Application Instructions: Complete an online staff application and upload/attach the following: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest, Resume, and a list of 3 professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=196744": {"title": "Police Officer", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Police Officer Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Police Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Police Officer Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Police Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: Jan 23, 2026 Closes: Nov 11, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 196744 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: Under the supervision of the police sergeant, the police officer's main function is to prevent and suppresses criminal activity and to ensure a safe and secure learning environment on campus.\u00a0 In addition, the police officer enforces governmental laws and regulations as well as university policies and procedures; perform police, traffic, crime prevention, and other duties.\u00a0 The police officer is responsible to safeguard all university assets, enforce traffic and parking regulations, investigates vehicle accidents and enforces Federal, state, and local laws as well as university regulations and policies. Performance Metrics: Patrol Effectiveness and Visibility Metric: Completes assigned foot, bike, and vehicular patrols across designated campus areas with high visibility and proactive engagement. Incident Response and Report Accuracy Metric: Responds to calls for service, including medical, criminal, and traffic incidents in a timely, professional manner and produces accurate and complete documentation. Policy Compliance and Community Service Metric: Demonstrates knowledge and consistent enforcement of university policies, laws, and ordinances while maintaining a service-oriented approach with students, staff, and visitors. Essential Functions: 1. Assist as panel a member during interview boards. 2. Assists the university community and visitors by providing general information. 3. Conduct courtesy services such but not limited to battery jump-starts, opening locked vehicles, and airing tires. 4. Conduct parameter patrol on Our Lady of the Lake Convent, McCollough and Regen Hall. 5. Enforces federal, state, and local laws and ordinances and University regulations and policies. 6. Investigates traffic accidents and criminal offenses and prepares investigation and special reports. 7. Makes arrests and appear in court as direct 8. Monitors and provides traffic and parking enforcement 9. Monitors external grounds lighting and generates work orders for light replacement when needed. 10. Opens and closes buildings, turns light on and off as needed. 11. Prevents and suppresses crime by being highly visible and by performing aggressive and continuous foot, bike and vehicular patrol. 12. Provide escorts on campus when directed to 13. Provides security surveillance of university facilities. 14. Responds and assist with all emergency detentions 15. Responds to all medical emergencies and is First Aid/CPR and AED certified Additional Responsibilities: Performs other related duties as assigned by a supervisor. Working Conditions: Work is performed in both office and field settings on a rotating shift schedule in all weather conditions. Tools and Equipment Used: Patrol vehicle, police radio, handgun, less than non-lethal weapons as required, handcuffs, first aid equipment, and personal computer including word processing software. Requirements: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by a police officer to successfully perform the essential functions of this job which are as follows: sit, talk, hear, stand, walk, run, use hands and fingers, handle or operate objects,\u00a0 reach with hands and arms; climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl, taste and smell.\u00a0 The police officer may be required to carry, drag, or restrain individuals from 50 to 300 pounds and lift in excess of 50 pounds.\u00a0 Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Hazards: Conditions present high stress and threat to personal safety during periods of search, seizure and arrest; may be exposed to toxic materials, blood-borne pathogens and other infectious environments; have to deal with unruly or dangerous individuals, unsafe building sites and the use deadly force; may be required to extend work schedule during university emergency situations as deemed necessary to ensure public safety by the Chief of Police. Emergency Essential Personnel / Positions (EEPP): The position of Police Officer is listed as a first responder and an emergency essential personal / position for Our Lady of the Lake University.\u00a0 EEPP positions shall be required to perform key duties and requirements during a crisis and emergencies on OLLU campuses. This entails a temporary or permanent relocation or redeployment between campuses as well as the possibility of remaining in an area when extreme hazardous conditions have occurred, could occurred or may occurred.\u00a0 Upon accepting a position as an EEPP with Our Lady of the Lake Police Department, you agree and accept to be recalled by the Chief of Police during all campus emergencies and will fulfill these duties and responsibilities due to the mission essential nature of EEPP positions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Ability to be on call 24 hrs. / 7 days a week and be able to respond to all campus emergencies as directed by the Chief of Police through the Lieutenant and Police Sergeant. 2. Ability to be on call 24 hrs. / 7 days a week and can respond to all campus emergencies as directed by the Chief of Police through the Lieutenant and Police Sergeant. 3. Ability to accomplish tasks in a professional and expeditious manner. 4. Ability to demonstrate sound judgment and possess good communication skills. 5. Ability to successfully complete the handgun, shotgun and patrol rifle qualifications. 6. Ability to successfully complete the TCOLE required physical exam, psychological exam, and drug screen. 7. Ability to work and cover half or full shift in the event of manpower shortage with limited notification and subject to shift rotations. 8. Ability to work holidays and required shift work to include days, evenings, nights and weekends. 9. Able to work under stressful situations Possess strong interpersonal skills (verbal and writing). 10. Dependability regarding handling work assignments and critical incidents. 11. Knowledge of Texas driving rules and regulations as evidenced by possession of current Texas driver's license. 12. Must be able to travel to the offsite campuses (San Antonio, Houston & La Feria) and be able to stay for an extended period. 13. Possess a basic knowledge of data entry and criminal report assessment. Education and Experience: High School graduate or GED required. Honorable discharge from military service (DD-2140) if applicable. Must have a Basic TCOLE peace officer's license. One year of experience required as a certified peace officer, preferably in a college/university environment. Valid Texas driver's license with good driving record required. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please submit online application and upload resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=196742": {"title": "Police Officer", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Police Officer Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Police Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Police Officer Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Police Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: Jan 23, 2026 Closes: Nov 11, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 196742 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: Under the supervision of the police sergeant, the police officer's main function is to prevent and suppresses criminal activity and to ensure a safe a