y performing aggressive and continuous foot, bike and vehicular patrol. 12. Provide escorts on campus when directed to 13. Provides security surveillance of university facilities. 14. Responds and assist with all emergency detentions 15. Responds to all medical emergencies and is First Aid/CPR and AED certified Additional Responsibilities: Performs other related duties as assigned by a supervisor. Working Conditions: Work is performed in both office and field settings on a rotating shift schedule in all weather conditions. Tools and Equipment Used: Patrol vehicle, police radio, handgun, less than non-lethal weapons as required, handcuffs, first aid equipment, and personal computer including word processing software. Requirements: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by a police officer to successfully perform the essential functions of this job which are as follows: sit, talk, hear, stand, walk, run, use hands and fingers, handle or operate objects,\u00a0 reach with hands and arms; climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl, taste and smell.\u00a0 The police officer may be required to carry, drag, or restrain individuals from 50 to 300 pounds and lift in excess of 50 pounds.\u00a0 Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Hazards: Conditions present high stress and threat to personal safety during periods of search, seizure and arrest; may be exposed to toxic materials, blood-borne pathogens and other infectious environments; have to deal with unruly or dangerous individuals, unsafe building sites and the use deadly force; may be required to extend work schedule during university emergency situations as deemed necessary to ensure public safety by the Chief of Police. Emergency Essential Personnel / Positions (EEPP): The position of Police Officer is listed as a first responder and an emergency essential personal / position for Our Lady of the Lake University.\u00a0 EEPP positions shall be required to perform key duties and requirements during a crisis and emergencies on OLLU campuses. This entails a temporary or permanent relocation or redeployment between campuses as well as the possibility of remaining in an area when extreme hazardous conditions have occurred, could occurred or may occurred.\u00a0 Upon accepting a position as an EEPP with Our Lady of the Lake Police Department, you agree and accept to be recalled by the Chief of Police during all campus emergencies and will fulfill these duties and responsibilities due to the mission essential nature of EEPP positions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Ability to be on call 24 hrs. / 7 days a week and be able to respond to all campus emergencies as directed by the Chief of Police through the Lieutenant and Police Sergeant. 2. Ability to be on call 24 hrs. / 7 days a week and can respond to all campus emergencies as directed by the Chief of Police through the Lieutenant and Police Sergeant. 3. Ability to accomplish tasks in a professional and expeditious manner. 4. Ability to demonstrate sound judgment and possess good communication skills. 5. Ability to successfully complete the handgun, shotgun and patrol rifle qualifications. 6. Ability to successfully complete the TCOLE required physical exam, psychological exam, and drug screen. 7. Ability to work and cover half or full shift in the event of manpower shortage with limited notification and subject to shift rotations. 8. Ability to work holidays and required shift work to include days, evenings, nights and weekends. 9. Able to work under stressful situations Possess strong interpersonal skills (verbal and writing). 10. Dependability regarding handling work assignments and critical incidents. 11. Knowledge of Texas driving rules and regulations as evidenced by possession of current Texas driver's license. 12. Must be able to travel to the offsite campuses (San Antonio, Houston & La Feria) and be able to stay for an extended period. 13. Possess a basic knowledge of data entry and criminal report assessment. Education and Experience: High School graduate or GED required. Honorable discharge from military service (DD-2140) if applicable. Must have a Basic TCOLE peace officer's license. One year of experience required as a certified peace officer, preferably in a college/university environment. Valid Texas driver's license with good driving record required. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please submit online application and upload resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=192544": {"title": "Police Officer", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Police Officer Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Police Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Police Officer Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Police Locations: SAN ANTONIO, TX Posted: Sep 5, 2025 Closes: Nov 11, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 192544 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: Under the supervision of the police sergeant, the police officer's main function is to prevent and suppresses criminal activity and to ensure a safe and secure learning environment on campus.\u00a0 In addition, the police officer enforces governmental laws and regulations as well as university policies and procedures; perform police, traffic, crime prevention, and other duties.\u00a0 The police officer is responsible to safeguard all university assets, enforce traffic and parking regulations, investigates vehicle accidents and enforces Federal, state, and local laws as well as university regulations and policies. Performance Metrics: Patrol Effectiveness and Visibility Metric: Completes assigned foot, bike, and vehicular patrols across designated campus areas with high visibility and proactive engagement. Incident Response and Report Accuracy Metric: Responds to calls for service?including medical, criminal, and traffic incidents?in a timely, professional manner and produces accurate and complete documentation. Policy Compliance and Community Service Metric: Demonstrates knowledge and consistent enforcement of university policies, laws, and ordinances while maintaining a service-oriented approach with students, staff, and visitors. Essential Functions: 1. Assist as panel a member during interview boards. 2. Assists the university community and visitors by providing general information. 3. Conduct courtesy services such but not limited to battery jump-starts, opening locked vehicles, and airing tires. 4. Conduct parameter patrol on Our Lady of the Lake Convent, McCollough and Regen Hall. 5. Enforces federal, state, and local laws and ordinances and University regulations and policies. 6. Investigates traffic accidents and criminal offenses and prepares investigation and special reports. 7. Makes arrests and appear in court as direct 8. Monitors and provides traffic and parking enforcement 9. Monitors external grounds lighting and generates work orders for light replacement when needed. 10. Opens and closes buildings, turns light on and off as needed. 11. Prevents and suppresses crime by being highly visible and by performing aggressive and continuous foot, bike and vehicular patrol. 12. Provide escorts on campus when directed to 13. Provides security surveillance of university facilities. 14. Responds and assist with all emergency detentions 15. Responds to all medical emergencies and is First Aid/CPR and AED certified Additional Responsibilities: Performs other related duties as assigned by a supervisor. Working Conditions: Work is performed in both office and field settings on a rotating shift schedule in all weather conditions. Tools and Equipment Used: Patrol vehicle, police radio, handgun, less than non-lethal weapons as required, handcuffs, first aid equipment, and personal computer including word processing software. Requirements: Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by a police officer to successfully perform the essential functions of this job which are as follows: sit, talk, hear, stand, walk, run, use hands and fingers, handle or operate objects,\u00a0 reach with hands and arms; climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl, taste and smell.\u00a0 The police officer may be required to carry, drag, or restrain individuals from 50 to 300 pounds and lift in excess of 50 pounds.\u00a0 Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Hazards: Conditions present high stress and threat to personal safety during periods of search, seizure and arrest; may be exposed to toxic materials, blood-borne pathogens and other infectious environments; have to deal with unruly or dangerous individuals, unsafe building sites and the use deadly force; may be required to extend work schedule during university emergency situations as deemed necessary to ensure public safety by the Chief of Police. Emergency Essential Personnel / Positions (EEPP): The position of Police Officer is listed as a first responder and an emergency essential personal / position for Our Lady of the Lake University.\u00a0 EEPP positions shall be required to perform key duties and requirements during a crisis and emergencies on OLLU campuses. This entails a temporary or permanent relocation or redeployment between campuses as well as the possibility of remaining in an area when extreme hazardous conditions have occurred, could occurred or may occurred.\u00a0 Upon accepting a position as an EEPP with Our Lady of the Lake Police Department, you agree and accept to be recalled by the Chief of Police during all campus emergencies and will fulfill these duties and responsibilities due to the mission essential nature of EEPP positions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to be on call 24 hrs. / 7 days a week and be able to respond to all campus emergencies as directed by the Chief of Police through the Lieutenant and Police Sergeant. Ability to be on call 24 hrs. / 7 days a week and can respond to all campus emergencies as directed by the Chief of Police through the Lieutenant and Police Sergeant. Ability to accomplish tasks in a professional and expeditious manner. Ability to demonstrate sound judgment and possess good communication skills. Ability to successfully complete the handgun, shotgun and patrol rifle qualifications. Ability to successfully complete the TCOLE required physical exam, psychological exam, and drug screen. Ability to work and cover half or full shift in the event of manpower shortage with limited notification and subject to shift rotations. Ability to work holidays and required shift work to include days, evenings, nights and weekends. Able to work under stressful situations Possess strong interpersonal skills (verbal and writing). Dependability regarding handling work assignments and critical incidents. Knowledge of Texas driving rules and regulations as evidenced by possession of current Texas driver's license. Must be able to travel to the offsite campuses (San Antonio, Houston & La Feria) and be able to stay for an extended period. Possess a basic knowledge of data entry and criminal report assessment. Education and Experience: 1. High School graduate or GED required. 2. Honorable discharge from military service (DD-2140) if applicable. 3. Must have a Basic TCOLE peace officer's license. 4. Valid Texas driver's license with good driving record required. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please submit online application and upload resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204339": {"title": "Preventative Maintenance Technician", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Preventative Maintenance Technician Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Preventative Maintenance Technician Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Preventative Maintenance Technician Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Sep 1, 2026 Closes: Dec 31, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 204339 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: PERFORMANCE EVALUATION METRICS: Efficiency - Ability to efficiently work with minimal direction Effectiveness - Ability to multi-task in fast pace environment. Quality - Produce quality work with minimal errors, attention to detail. Attendance - Reliable and strong, provides notice for absences. Under the supervision of the Preventive Maintenance Supervisor, performs preventive maintenance on designated machinery and filtration systems. Assists the Preventive Maintenance Supervisor in servicing the University fire extinguishers. Assist in repairing kitchen equipment and elevators. Performs other duties assigned by the Maintenance Superintendent or Preventive Maintenance Supervisor ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Performs preventive maintenance on the heating, refrigeration, and air conditioning systems on campus, including oiling and greasing machinery; cleaning and changing filters; adjusting and replacing bulbs and cleaning strainers and traps. Assist in stock inventory of all departmental items. Maintains equipment records for scheduling of maintenance and monitors systems performance with continuous attention to malfunction and repair needs. Performs minor repairs on mechanical systems. Elevators, and kitchen equipment. Maintains university fire extinguishers and a service log on such equipment. Assists Preventive Maintenance Supervisor in responding to emergency and critical situations. Maintains quality and neatness of all University preventive maintenance jobs. Coordinates wok with other trades, maintenance a proper relationship with assigned personnel, other workmen, department personnel and personnel outside Facilities Management. Complete all assignments in a professional manner, as rapidly and responsibly as possible while maintaining high quality. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITITES: Works inside and outside, in dusty, noisy places. Ability to work in tight high places. Ability to lift, carry, push or pull a variety of tools, equipment and materials. Ability to climb, balance, stoop, kneel and crouch. Ability to lift approximately 75 pounds and with assistance lift in excess of 100 pounds. Ability to work in high places on ladders, scaffolding, and roof tops. Ability to operate power tools. Knowledge of heating, refrigeration, and air conditioning tools. Requirements: EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Two (2) year experience in the field of preventive maintenance, general maintenance, or specific trade field\u00a0\u00a0 with evidence of having consistently performed general maintenance work at an acceptable level, required. Must have a valid Texas driver's license and a good driving record. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Employment and attach a Cover Letter and CV or Resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205964": {"title": "Residence Life Coordinator", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Residence Life Coordinator Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Residence Life Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Residence Life Coordinator Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residence Life Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Oct 20, 2026 Closes: Dec 8, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 205964 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: With the guidance of the Director (DRL) and Assistant Director (ADRL) of Residence Life, the Residence Life Coordinator (RLC) supports the residential experience and student development while providing day-to-day operational leadership for an assigned residence hall area. The RLC supervises and develops Resident Assistants (RAs), supports retention and recruitment efforts, coordinates residence hall operations and facilities concerns, responds to emergencies, and collaborates with campus partners to promote a safe, inclusive, and engaging living-learning environment. The RLC is expected to exercise independent judgment, maintain accurate and comprehensive records, address and resolve complex student concerns effectively, and leverage housing and conduct data to identify opportunities for operational improvements and student success. The coordinator receives a salary, furnished on-campus apartment, and meal plan as part of their compensation package. Performance Evaluation Metrics: Resident Satisfaction - Through written and verbal feedback, residents will share positive responsiveness to student needs, community building, and creating a safe living and learning environment. Resident Assistant Supervision - Performance and feedback of RA's that show the effectiveness of RLC supervisor communication and training with RAs. Operational and Compliance Performance - Timely completion of housing operations, health and safety processes, work orders, documentation, and required reports, with accurate records and follow-through. Essential Functions: Major responsibilities of the RLC include assisting in the supervision of Resident Assistant (RA) staff, assisting in the development and implementation of student development programming, providing administrative support for hall operations, and assuming primary responsibility for a residence hall area. Student Resident Support Serves in the regular \"on-call\" supervisory rotation and responds to emergencies, crises, safety concerns, and incidents affecting residential students and facilities, while observing safety and risk management measures. Ensure the safety of the students by reporting issues, tracking key inventory, working with the University Police Department (UPD), and enforcing the rules outlined in the resident handbook and student handbook. Work cooperatively with other campus units such as UPD, Counseling Services, Student Involvement, and Student Affairs to ensure the delivery of essential services to students. Mediate roommate conflicts that escalate beyond the Resident Assistant's intervention efforts. Resident Assistant Staff Assist with recruiting, interviewing, selecting, training, supervising, and evaluating RA staff. Supervise and support assigned RAs by reviewing, evaluating, and approving program plans and bulletin board submissions; providing constructive guidance on programming initiatives and content; monitoring compliance with established deadlines and expectations; and assessing program effectiveness. Conduct group weekly meetings and bi-weekly one-on-one meetings with RA staff. Coordinate the RA on-duty schedule (for their area). Coordinate the RA desk schedule for all RAs. Administrative Functions Assist ADRL with coordination of health and safety inspections, residential education programming, and larger dept community building programs. Assist with resident check-in/check-out in StarRez and ID activation in Velocity Assist with maintaining departmental procedures, calendars, tracking systems, reports, and documentation for assigned areas. Track RA programs, health and safety checks, and other required data for reports on their assigned area. Assist with the reporting, investigation, and management of Title IX and student conduct matters, roommate conflicts, policy violations, and student concerns as instructed; ensure appropriate and timely documentation, communication, follow-up, and referral. Create social media content and post after approval; monitor department social media and respond appropriately. Follow processes for key inventory, hall access, emergency response, and security practices. Effectively communicate with the DRL about any issues or concerns regarding residents, residence life staff, and the residence hall; follow up on student retention alerts and report findings to the DRL. Learn and utilize the housing occupancy management software system (StarRez); keep accurate records of resident information. Represents the interests of the University and the DRL in all RA personnel and resident matters. Attend all division meetings and seminars as scheduled and attend weekly and impromptu meetings with the Residence Life pro staff. Facilities Management Oversee daily hall operations within the assigned residential area, including conducting routine facility walkthroughs, coordinating and monitoring work orders through completion, facilitating timely communication with residents, and maintaining a consistent and visible staff presence. Coordinates with Facilities, housekeeping, vendors, and other campus partners regarding maintenance, work orders, repairs, and residence hall conditions; follows up on unresolved issues. Complete furniture inventory and damage reports for Residence Life areas at the end of the school year or as needed. Assist with replacing furniture at the end of the school year. Additional Responsibilities: Serve on committees established by the Office of Residence Life (training, program recognition, community development, etc.), as well as any other university committees that may benefit from the input of a Residence Life perspective. Become acquainted with and remain knowledgeable of University services, offices, and information in the Residence Life staff manual and resident handbook. Assist the DRL, ADRL, and/or Office Manager in designated projects and the administration of all summer camps, conferences, and groups visiting the university and utilizing the residence halls. Provides support for Lake Day Orientation, Blue Nation Welcome, and other Student Affairs events. Participates in other university activities and programs as requested and assigned. Performs other related duties as assigned by the ADRL, DRL, Assistant Vice President for Student Affairs, or Vice President for Student Affairs. Requirements: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to live on-campus and encompass a rotational, evening/weekend \"on call\" supervisory responsibility. Ability to work flexible hours, with busier periods at certain times of the semester, including nights, weekends, holidays, and on-call responsibilities as needed. Ability to write and communicate effectively. Ability to exercise independent and sound judgment and respond to a crisis under pressure. Ability to handle sensitive issues and correspondence with confidentiality and discretion. Ability to effectively use Microsoft Office and other university Windows-based software. Ability to learn the housing software in a timely manner. Ability to meet the OLLU and Residence Life staff standards for on-campus and workplace environment safety for self and any family or guests on property. Ability to lift at least 20 pounds and be able to quickly move between housing buildings during emergencies. Must be able to perform essential job duties across multiple campus facilities and building floors, including older buildings that may have limited accessibility and no elevator service. Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree required. Required minimum of one year experience in housing/residence life, housing management, or other Student Affairs area, preferably in a university setting; student experience is applicable. Experience planning and implementing campus student programs. Must live on-campus in the furnished apartment. Application Instructions: Complete an online staff application and upload/attach the following:\u00a0Cover Letter/Letter of Interest, Resume, and a list of 3 professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204106": {"title": "Senior Associate Director of Graduate Admissions", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Senior Associate Director of Graduate Admissions Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Senior Associate Director of Graduate Admissions Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Associate Director of Graduate Admissions Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Enrollment Management Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Oct 28, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 204106 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: OLLU seeks an experienced, mission-driven Senior Associate Director of Graduate Admissions to lead recruitment and enrollment efforts across the university's graduate portfolio, including master's and doctoral programs offered in San Antonio, Houston, and the Rio Grande Valley, as well as online. Reporting to the Dean of Admissions, the Senior Associate Director owns the full graduate recruitment cycle, from inquiry through enrollment, for OLLU's predominantly domestic graduate population, while helping build toward a small but strategically important international graduate presence over time. The ideal candidate is a hands-on leader who builds strong partnerships with academic program directors, champions prospective students through every step of their journey, and reflects OLLU's commitment to access, opportunity, and the communities it serves. Performance Evaluation Metrics: Recruitment & Yield: Achieve graduate enrollment targets across OLLU's program portfolio; maintain strong conversion rates from inquiry through application, admission, and enrollment. Program Partnership: Build effective, trusted working relationships with graduate program directors and faculty to align recruitment activity with program capacity and academic priorities. Pipeline Development: Establish and grow sustainable domestic pipelines, including employer partnerships, alumni referral, and an undergraduate-to-graduate bridge, while laying the groundwork for measured international growth. Operational Excellence: Ensure strong Slate data integrity and self-sufficiency; partner with the Director of Enrollment Operations and Analytics to build efficient, student-centered workflows. Essential Functions: 1. Recruitment Strategy and Execution Own graduate enrollment targets and translate OLLU's graduate enrollment strategy into a detailed, program-specific recruitment and yield plan covering master's and doctoral programs across San Antonio, Houston, and the Rio Grande Valley, as well as online and professional programs; drive disciplined execution every cycle. Develop and manage the annual graduate recruitment calendar, coordinating in-person and virtual events, webinars, chat sessions, employer information sessions, and graduate/professional fairs. Carry a personal recruitment portfolio, maintaining direct relationships with prospective students, employers, and referral sources, and modeling the standards expected of the team. Use Slate, enrollment analytics, and AI-enabled tools to monitor pipeline health and program-level performance, and maintain recruitment reporting, including ROI tracking, for review with the Dean of Admissions. Create and execute lead-nurturing communication and social media campaigns, in partnership with the Enrollment Communications Manager and MarCom, that move prospective students efficiently from inquiry to enrolled. Partner with the Assistant Director of Campus Visit and Student Experience to build a compelling admitted-student experience, including open houses, campus visits, tours, and program-specific yield communications. Serve as a thought partner to the Dean of Admissions in scoping a measured international graduate recruitment strategy, coordinating with the PDSO as needed. Ensure an unparalleled customer service experience for all prospective students throughout the recruitment cycle. 2. Team Leadership and Development Lead, coach, and develop graduate admissions counselor(s), setting clear goals, maintaining accountability, and building a culture focused on results and student experience. Hire, train, and onboard graduate admissions counselor(s) as the team grows. Ensure the team is self-sufficient in Slate for all day-to-day tasks; maintain data entry standards and data integrity. Partner with the Director of Enrollment Operations and Analytics to build efficient, student-centered workflows. 3. Collaboration and Partnerships Collaborate closely with graduate program directors and academic deans across schools to align recruitment activity with program capacity, curriculum changes, and academic priorities, and to engage faculty directly in recruitment and yield activities such as webinars and info sessions. Partner with Financial Aid on graduate aid and scholarship strategy that supports access and meets net revenue goals. Partner with MarCom and academic program departments to ensure all graduate-facing web content stays current and accurate, and to develop program-specific marketing assets and student stories. Engage Alumni Relations and employer partners on recruitment, referral, and yield opportunities. 4. Analytics and Operations Develop and maintain graduate admissions policies, procedures, and operational workflows that ensure a smooth, equitable applicant experience; review and recommend updates to admissions criteria as needed. Maintain statistics on applicant demographics, program mix, and pipeline sources; use this data to refine recruitment strategy each cycle. Manage graduate admissions budget and vendor relationships with fiscal discipline, evaluating ROI and strategic fit across recruitment and yield activities. Additional Responsibilities: Other duties as assigned by the Dean of Admissions. Requirements: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Proven ability to build strong relationships with academic partners and lead recruitment execution with accountability for results. Strong analytical skills; proficiency in Slate or comparable CRM and familiarity with AI-enabled recruitment tools and emerging enrollment technology. Deep knowledge of graduate and adult/professional student recruitment, including online program recruitment; familiarity with the South Texas higher education landscape and the HSI student experience is a plus. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across a complex campus environment, including with faculty and academic program directors. Direct experience recruiting or advising international students strongly preferred. Ability to manage budgets and resources with fiscal discipline. Bilingual (English/Spanish) preferred. Education and Experience: Master's degree required in higher education, business, marketing, or a related field (required). Minimum of 5 to 7 years of progressive experience in graduate admissions or enrollment management at a mission-driven institution, with a demonstrated track record of meeting or exceeding enrollment goals (required). Experience with domestic recruitment strongly required; experience with international recruitment or international student support strongly preferred (required). Willingness to travel during peak recruitment seasons; availability for evening and weekend work is expected (required). Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Employment and attach a Cover Letter and CV or Resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202636": {"title": "Undergraduate Admissions Counselor", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Undergraduate Admissions Counselor Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Enrollment Management Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Jul 14, 2026 Closes: Oct 28, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 202636 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Join OLLU's Undergraduate Admissions team and help shape the next generation of Saints. As an Admissions Counselor, you'll own a territory of high schools and community colleges, from a student's first inquiry to their first day on campus. You'll travel, present, review and decide on applications, and use data and CRM tools to guide students through the process, building the relationships that help them choose where to spend the next four years. This is a full-cycle recruitment role with real ownership from day one, and a clear runway for someone looking to build a career in college admissions. Performance Evaluation Metrics: Territory Pipeline Health: Own your territory like an account manager owns their relationships ? keep prospect and applicant records current in Slate, and report on territory pipeline metrics weekly. Application Volume & Conversion: Grow inquiries into applications and applications into admits across your territory, using data to identify where to focus your time and contributing to OLLU's overall enrollment goals each cycle. Yield & Melt Prevention: Guide admitted students to enrollment through proactive outreach, using data-driven tools to identify students who may be at risk of melting, and stay connected with them through to their first day. Recruitment Activity: Complete your assigned school visits, college fairs, and community events each fall and spring recruitment season. Requirements: Territory Recruitment Manage an assigned territory of high schools, ISDs, and/or community colleges, building relationships with counselors and advisors. Conduct in-school visits, college fairs, and community outreach throughout the fall (Aug-Nov) and spring (Jan-Mar) recruitment seasons, including some overnight travel. Serve as the primary OLLU contact for prospects and families in your territory, from inquiry through enrollment. Develop territory-specific recruitment strategies in collaboration with admissions leadership to meet enrollment goals. Maintain accurate, current records for all prospects and applicants in Slate CRM. Advise students and families on OLLU's merit and need-based scholarships and guide them through FAFSA completion. Partner with Financial Aid to co-attend key recruitment events and family financial aid nights, ensuring students and families get clear, consistent guidance on cost and affordability. Application Review & Admissions Decisions Review undergraduate applications for completeness and academic eligibility per OLLU admissions requirements. Make admissions decisions for freshman and transfer applicants, escalating exceptions to the Associate Director. Communicate admissions decisions and scholarship awards to students in a timely, personalized manner. Process dual credit, AP, and IB credit documentation in coordination with the Registrar's Office. Yield & Melt Prevention Reach out proactively to admitted students to guide them toward enrollment, through calls, texts, and event invitations. Monitor deposited students through the summer, following up with anyone who needs support completing next steps. Participate in all Lake Day Orientation (LDO) sessions, supporting students through the admitted-to-enrolled transition. Additional Responsibilities: Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: High energy and comfortable putting yourself out there ? you'll be meeting new people every day, whether that's a single student or a room full of families. Comfortable with verbal and written communication, including presenting to individuals and large groups. Ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, and relationships in a fast-paced recruitment environment. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; experience with Slate CRM or demonstrated willingness to learn quickly. Commitment to building authentic relationships with first-generation college students. Bilingual English/Spanish preferred, given OLLU's HSI designation and student population. Knowledge of the San Antonio, Houston, or Central Texas educational landscape is a plus. Valid driver's license required. This role requires regular travel within the assigned territory, including some evenings, weekends, and overnight trips during fall and spring recruitment seasons. Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution, any field, required. One or more years of experience in a customer-facing, sales, or relationship-driven role, including internships, campus leadership, or part-time work, required. Experience in higher education admissions or student affairs is a plus but not required. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the online Application for Employment and attach\u00a0a Cover Letter and CV or Resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=101918": {"title": "Professional Science Tutor (POOL)", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Professional Science Tutor (POOL) Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Professional Science Tutor (POOL) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Professional Science Tutor (POOL) Category: Staff Part Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Center for Excellence Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Aug 24, 2018 Closes: Nov 1, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 101918 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: Provide one-on-one and some group tutoring for students in science courses, especially in Chemistry and Biology; participate in training and team meetings; and complete administrative forms and reports. Typical workload is approximately 10-15 hours per week between the hours of 10:00 a.m. and 10:00 p.m. Essential Functions: Tutors students in the sciences, courses such as General Chemistry, Organic & Inorganic Chemistry, Physical Science, Physics, General Biology, Molecular Biology, Anatomy & Physiology. Maintains accurate updated records for appointments. Attends all meetings and professional development sessions Reports concerns and other relevant information to ACE Director Serves as a resource person for students in the sciences Serves as a liaison with various Faculty members and ACE to increase tutoring services for students. Participates in student workshops as needed. Additional Responsibilities: May be required to work weekends and/or evenings for special events. May need to conduct library or Internet research relevant to ACE programs. Performs other duties and responsibilities as relevant to science tutoring. Requirements: Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Positive attitude about learning and enjoys student interactions. Ability to work with minimal supervision and manage multiple tasks. Excellent oral, written communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Ability to maintain a high degree of confidentiality. Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree, with upper division science courses, required. Experience with tutoring, specifically at the college level, required Employment is contingent on a successful background investigation. Additional Information: Minimum Starting Rate: $13-15 hourly, depending on experience and/or degree.\u00a0 About 10-15 hours per week Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the On-Line Staff Application, attach a resume, cover letter,\u00a0 and course transcripts (unofficial for initial interview). Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206138": {"title": "Office Manager Community Counseling Service", "description": "Our Lady of the Lake University\nJob Posting: Office Manager Community Counseling Service Our Lady of the Lake University \n\tJob Posting: Office Manager Community Counseling Service Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Office Manager Community Counseling Service Category: Staff Full Time Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: San Antonio, TX Posted: Oct 26, 2026 Closes: Dec 14, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Position\u00a0ID: 206138 Share About Our Lady of the Lake University: On a foundation of faith, wisdom and trust in Divine Providence, Our Lady of the Lake University (OLLU) empowers graduates to transform their communities, families, and professions. Founded in 1895 by the Sisters of Divine Providence, OLLU stands as San Antonio's oldest regionally accredited institution of higher learning. A private, Catholic university, it currently enrolls approximately 1,800 students across undergraduate and graduate programs. With its main residential campus in San Antonio and additional locations in Houston and the Rio Grande Valley (La Feria), and online programs, OLLU extends its mission across Texas, the border region, and the nation. Academic Programs OLLU offers a rich academic portfolio of more than 30 undergraduate majors and minors, 14 master's programs and three doctoral programs. Courses are delivered through diverse formats to support traditional and non-traditional students alike. Job Description: Job Summary: Provides administrative support to the Director of the Community Counseling Service and to oversee office activities. Performance Metrics: Must maintain the highest levels of Confidentiality -At all times Must greet students and clients with respect and professionalism at all times Must manage Clinic operations, including ordering billing and logistics Essential Functions: 1. Performs receptionist duties in the office of CCS such as greeting visitors, answering telephone inquiries and routing incoming calls and checks voicemail to return inquiries. Checks in clients and makes appointments/return appointments. Crisis calls are monitored and directed appropriately. 2. Assists the Clinic Director with day-to-day operations of the Community Counseling Service. 3. Inventories and prepares requisitions for Supervisors, Students, Graduate Assistants with equipment and office supplies. Liaison to the Help Desk for technical difficulties; computers and printer. 4. Performs data entry tasks. Administers access to Titanium for all Users. 5. Prepares and updates the CCS budget report. 6. Prepares PO's for monthly billing to various accounts. 7. Reviews service receipts and prepares bank deposits of client service fees. 8. Maintains contracts to insurance companies. Quarterly updates the CAQH credentialing for all insurance companies. 9. Bills client insurance. 10. Maintains continuous inventory of office supplies and supplies Clinic with needed materials. 11. Assists with the supervision/training of Graduate Assistants. 12. Coordinates virtual teletherapy appointments. Additional Responsibilities: 1. Prepares Practicum Packets for students each semester. 2. Prepares clinic for teams each semester: a. Orders name tags b. Maintains Teams in My Outcomes. c. Organizes Teams at the Community Counseling Service Center schedules for students each semester. d. Checks Student Hour Logs each semester. 3. Supports Graduate Assistants: a. Hires and interview for Graduate Assistants b. Trains and Supervise GA's. c. Maintains employment forms for GA's. d. Provides Graduate Assistants access to Titanium and the CCS email which is then maintained and supervised. e. Schedules and budgets for the allotted GA's for CCS. f. Maintains the Performance Evaluations for each Graduate Assistant each semester. 4. Serves as first point of contact when subpoenas are issued. 5. Distributes client intakes, schedules appointment and sets fee. 6. Inputs client demographic data into Titanium/Teams. 7. Facilitates the evaluation process at the end of each semester. 8. Delivers mail and checks Post Office on campus for mail. 9. Liaison with Lessor of the building. Arranges for pest control, light outages, housekeeping issues and damages to property. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Maintains confidentiality- demonstrates respect and compassion 2. Effective oral and written communication skills. 3. Proficiency in the use of relevant office computer applications. 4. Ability to prioritize and organize multiple, simultaneous projects. 5. Ability to perform tedious tasks and other work with precision and accuracy in a timely manner. 6. Ability to use office equipment, such as copy machine, printers, fax machines, etc. 7. Knowledge or mental health billing a plus. Requirements: 1. Two years of experience in a secretary or an administrative assistant role. (Substantial related billing experience may be considered in lieu of secretary or admin support experience.) 2. Mental health billing experience strongly desired. 3. 60 college credit hours preferred. Additional Information: Employment with Our Lady of the Lake University is contingent upon the applicant undergoing a background investigation. OLLU seeks to attract, develop and retain the highest quality faculty, staff and administrators. The University is committed to diversity and strongly encourages applications from women and minorities. EOE Our Lady of the Lake University uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Application Instructions: Please complete the On-Line Staff Application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Our Lady of the Lake University 411 S.W. 24th Street\n\t\t\t\t\tSan Antonio, Texas 78207"}}, "rows": {"https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=62108": {"school_id": 1423, "posting_url": "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=62108", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor of Accounting", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Business and Leadership", "area_key_words": "Accounting; weekend classes Prior experience working", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "Jul 30, 2015", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=81252": {"school_id": 1423, "posting_url": "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=81252", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor of Applied Social and Cultural Sciences", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Applied Social and Cultural Sciences; Sociology program", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "Feb 7, 2017", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=47360": {"school_id": 1423, "posting_url": "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=47360", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor of Art (multiple positions)", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Art", "deadline_of_application": "November 20, 2014", "posted_date": "Mar 11, 2014", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=46957": {"school_id": 1423, "posting_url": "https://ollusa.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=46957", "job_title_in_pos